,"position":{"commit_sha":"3a7e13bdfd5bb619f66a8eb643ff89a51b834ec9","position":"1785350220962494001-171fff41-cd7c-4aee-b7d0-4c8b21b3fd4f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"dce01392aa7062e9bd39f777f33e486f0c1e7dd52a4f40bba305cebb10804dfa","event_uuid":"9dae72ad-a08b-4f12-acef-f6f831c6d008","position":{"commit_sha":"f7feed0892be86056a61869b506c5ea0b1e24dba","position":"1785350239662657001-9dae72ad-a08b-4f12-acef-f6f831c6d008"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"11c35fa649a139c9cba4ab7c27d58fda62c5c0df76b8cec9666cc593560902f9","event_uuid":"9b81b5c6-33c5-4636-ae81-caee3184750a","position":{"commit_sha":"aad8a09ae500a290cee07fbae21efb1192e1e1ab","position":"1785350387667549001-9b81b5c6-33c5-4636-ae81-caee3184750a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7ea6c0b2376d0e0738a25f998e6893159faacd04d2108835b33641b44dc043ec","event_uuid":"52395bc4-123e-4870-942f-06dd5a4b424a","position":{"commit_sha":"382493e5fd370996baf2f42038d4f1c64a1ad368","position":"1785350422975172001-52395bc4-123e-4870-942f-06dd5a4b424a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"46b5bd96017ce89425b4fac8a9d22a7dab178dcebc3373add464e05ba5c3907c","event_uuid":"e2e4d8ef-f148-4850-8237-b5fa41b20cef","position":{"commit_sha":"720c421f23760820858eb99a284a65e1e3086551","position":"1785350424400438001-e2e4d8ef-f148-4850-8237-b5fa41b20cef"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"duplicate","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"DUPLICATE of epic e594-e1d0-74f4-4d40 (bronze-used-foxhound), 'Bound tickets-repo growth: shrink reconciler .bridge_state on-branch', which is TABLED at status=idea and already contains a far more thorough analysis — including the same root cause (baseline_advanced_at as a write-only timestamp bumped unconditionally every pass), four history dossiers on why the current design exists, and a sequenced 4-step plan.\n\nClosing in favour of e594. The fresh measurements from this ticket have been posted as a comment there: the problem has more than doubled since e594 was tabled (bridge_state 375 MB -> 942.5 MB; bindings.json 987 -> 3,009 versions), and aggressive repack has been ruled out as a lever (8,157 of 8,165 bridge-state blobs are already deltified at avg depth 13.9).","timestamp":1785350239662657001}],"created_at":1785350110957617001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"171fff41-cd7c-4aee-b7d0-4c8b21b3fd4f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e594-e1d0-74f4-4d40"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nMeasured while answering 'how do we safely reduce the 1.02 GiB packed .git'. The tickets and their sidecars are NOT the problem. The Jira reconciler's bridge state is.\n\n## Measured pack composition (pack-b2b621b8, 212,856 objects)\n\n| content | packed |\n|---|---|\n| `.bridge_state/bindings.json` | **739.8 MB** (3,009 blobs, avg 252 KB) |\n| `.bridge_state/prev_snapshot.json` | **202.7 MB** (5,151 blobs, avg 40 KB) |\n| ALL real ticket events (SNAPSHOT/COMMENT/EDIT/CREATE/STATUS/LINK/...) | ~14 MB |\n| REVIEW_RESULT sidecars | 24.5 MB |\n| code + everything else | 25.9 MB |\n\nBridge state is **942.5 MB of a 1.03 GiB pack (91%)**. Working-tree sizes: `bindings.json` 17 MB, `prev_snapshot.json` 26 MB - two large single files rewritten in full on every reconcile.\n\n## Root cause of the churn (measured on two consecutive revisions)\n\nBetween consecutive writes the file grows only **+2,470 bytes**, and only **1,229 added / 1,166 deleted lines out of 526,487 (0.45%)**. But of those ~2,395 changed lines, **2,290 are `baseline_advanced_at` timestamp updates** - 96%% of the churn. The remaining ~69 lines are real change (`type`, `text`, `last_get_pass`).\n\nIn one file version there are 1,507 `baseline_advanced_at` occurrences with 230 distinct values - but **1,145 of them carry the SAME value**, bumped together on each pass. It is one logical fact (this pass advanced the baseline at time T) physically duplicated across ~1,145 binding entries.\n\nThe field is only 0.4%% of the file's bytes, but the edits are SCATTERED across all 18 MB, so every reconcile produces a delta with ~1,145 separate change regions. That is what defeats delta compression and yields 252 KB packed per version.\n\n## Why the obvious remedies do not work\n\n- **Aggressive repack will not help materially.** The blobs are ALREADY deltified: 8,157 of 8,165 bridge-state blobs have delta depth > 0 (avg depth 13.9) and still occupy 940.5 MB. Only 8 blobs (1.9 MB) are non-deltified. There is essentially no delta headroom left.\n- **`git gc`** reclaims only the 3 stray `tmp_pack_*` files (3.67 MiB) and consolidates 14 packs. Free, but small.\n- **History rewrite** would reclaim the most but is unsafe: `tickets` is the shared source of truth and rewriting it breaks every clone.\n\n## Fix direction (stops the bleeding; safe, no history rewrite)\n\nStop rewriting a per-binding field that is really one global fact:\n1. Hoist `baseline_advanced_at` to a single top-level value (per pass), leaving per-binding entries untouched when nothing about that binding changed; or\n2. only update a binding's `baseline_advanced_at` when that binding actually changed.\n\nEither collapses per-reconcile churn from ~2,395 changed lines to ~69, which should cut new-version delta cost by roughly 97%%.\n\nWorth considering alongside: whether `prev_snapshot.json` (26 MB, 5,151 versions, 202 MB packed) needs to be versioned at all, or is a derived cache that could live outside git.\n\n## Status: DUPLICATE — superseded by epic e594-e1d0-74f4-4d40\n\nThis ticket was filed before discovering `e594-e1d0-74f4-4d40` (bronze-used-foxhound),\n\"Bound tickets-repo growth: shrink reconciler .bridge_state on-branch\", which is TABLED at\nstatus=idea and already contains a more thorough analysis of the same problem — including the\nidentical root cause (`baseline_advanced_at` bumped unconditionally every pass), four history\ndossiers on why the current design exists, and a sequenced four-step plan.\n\nThe measurements gathered here have been transferred to e594 as a comment, where they are\nuseful as an update: the problem has more than doubled since e594 was tabled, and aggressive\nrepack has been ruled out as a remedy.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] The measurements are recorded on the surviving ticket (posted as a comment on e594).\n- [x] This ticket is linked to e594 (`relates_to`) so the trail is discoverable.\n- [x] No implementation work is carried here; the fix is tracked by e594's plan.\n","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","e594-e1d0-74f4-4d40"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"52395bc4-123e-4870-942f-06dd5a4b424a","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["reconciler","git","repo-size","performance"],"ticket_id":"7f6c-df12-e3dc-4691","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Jira bridge state is 91% of the git pack: a per-binding timestamp is rewritten on every reconcile","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0c894e86-4be7-4606-9df3-48df5cd6837a","171fff41-cd7c-4aee-b7d0-4c8b21b3fd4f","9dae72ad-a08b-4f12-acef-f6f831c6d008","9b81b5c6-33c5-4636-ae81-caee3184750a","52395bc4-123e-4870-942f-06dd5a4b424a","e2e4d8ef-f148-4850-8237-b5fa41b20cef"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659627100523001,"uuid":"782ad8b3-5d00-4e26-a828-8044c3008dc8"}